{"name":"Jubilation","hex":"#fbdd24","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"jubilation","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A triumphant shouting of great happiness; rejoicing, especially as celebratory outbursts; a feeling of joyous exultation."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/jubilation"}],"entries":[{"title":"Jubilation!","blocks":[{"text":"Jubilation! was a daytime parade from Tokyo Disneyland that ran from 2008 to 2013."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jubilation!","wikidata":"Q6301778"},{"title":"Jubilation (The Band album)","blocks":[{"text":"Jubilation is the tenth and final studio album by Canadian/American rock group the Band. Recorded in the spring of 1998 in Levon Helm's home studio in Woodstock, New York, it was released on September 15, 1998. For the first time since the group reformed without guitarist and songwriter Robbie Robertson, there were more originals than covers. Songs include \"Last Train to Memphis\", featuring guest guitarist Eric Clapton, Garth Hudson's solo instrumental closer \"French Girls\", Rick Danko's \"High Cotton\" and the ode to Ronnie Hawkins, \"White Cadillac\"."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/f/f2/Jubilation_%28The_Band_album_-_cover_art%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jubilation_(The_Band_album)","wikidata":"Q3282465"},{"title":"Jubilation (song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Jubilation\" is a song recorded by Canadian singer-songwriter Paul Anka for his 1972 studio album of the same name. Anka wrote the song with Johnny Harris, who also produced the track. It was released in 1972 as a 7\" single by Buddah Records. A gospel song, the lyrics of \"Jubilation\" find the protagonist preaching about religious themes. Making a moderate commercial impact, it appeared on the record charts in both Canada and the United States. It has since been included on several of Anka's greatest hits albums and covered by The Edwin Hawkins Singers in 1973."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/2/2d/Paul_Anka_%22Jubilation%22.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jubilation_(song)","wikidata":"Q30598062"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/6/6c/Barbra_Streisand_%22Jubilation%22.jpg/250px-Barbra_Streisand_%22Jubilation%22.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/6/6c/Barbra_Streisand_%22Jubilation%22.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/6/6c/Barbra_Streisand_%22Jubilation%22.jpg/250px-Barbra_Streisand_%22Jubilation%22.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABarbra_Streisand_%22Jubilation%22.jpg"}],"sounds":{"jubilation":[{"type":"audio/wav","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/e/e8/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Y._Dongchen-jubilation.wav?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/e/e8/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Y._Dongchen-jubilation.wav/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Y._Dongchen-jubilation.wav.mp3"},{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/e/e8/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Y._Dongchen-jubilation.wav/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Y._Dongchen-jubilation.wav.ogg"}]},"pictures":[{"title":"Etymology of a Classical Meitei language term for “yellow colour”","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5e/Etymology_of_a_Classical_Meitei_language_term_for_%E2%80%9Cyellow_colour%E2%80%9D.jpg/500px-Etymology_of_a_Classical_Meitei_language_term_for_%E2%80%9Cyellow_colour%E2%80%9D.jpg","ratio":1.3333333333333333,"l